<main id="main-content" class="feature-page feature-detail-page">
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">ublock origin after chrome</span></nav>
  <section class="feature-hero feature-hero--detail feature-hero--text" aria-labelledby="ubo-chrome-title">
    <p class="section-kicker">after manifest v2</p>
    <h1 id="ubo-chrome-title">Chrome stopped running full uBlock Origin. Blanc still includes it.</h1>
    <p>Since Chrome 138 in July 2025, Chrome has disabled Manifest V2 extensions for every user, and on August 31, 2026 Google removed the remaining ones from the Chrome Web Store. The full uBlock Origin is a Manifest V2 extension. Blanc, a desktop browser built on Chromium, includes it as an optional blocker.</p>
    <a class="text-link" href="https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/develop/migrate/mv2-deprecation-timeline">Read Google’s Manifest V2 timeline <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </section>

  <section class="feature-copy-grid feature-copy-grid--top" aria-labelledby="ubo-chrome-what-title">
    <div><p class="section-kicker">what you get</p><h2 id="ubo-chrome-what-title">The full uBlock Origin, not a Lite version.</h2></div>
    <div class="feature-copy-list">
      <article><h3>The tools you used.</h3><p>Blanc includes uBlock Origin 1.75.0 with its popup, dashboard, logger, element picker, custom filters and filter-list subscriptions.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Filter lists still update.</h3><p>Filter lists can update on their own. uBlock Origin itself updates only with reviewed Blanc releases.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Not uBO Lite.</h3><p>uBlock Origin Lite is a separate extension its developers built on Chrome’s newer Manifest V3 API, and it filters declaratively. Blanc includes the original uBlock Origin.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/uBlockOrigin/uBOL-home">About uBlock Origin Lite <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="feature-copy-grid" aria-labelledby="ubo-chrome-switch-title">
    <div><p class="section-kicker">switching</p><h2 id="ubo-chrome-switch-title">Three steps to switch.</h2></div>
    <div class="feature-copy-list">
      <article><h3>1. Download Blanc.</h3><p>Blanc is free for macOS, Windows and Linux. <a href="/download">Download it here</a>.</p></article>
      <article><h3>2. Choose uBlock Origin from the shield.</h3><p>Click the shield on the island, choose uBlock Origin, then restart Blanc to apply it. Blanc Blocker stays the default until you switch.</p></article>
      <article><h3>3. Bring your settings, if you saved them.</h3><p>uBlock Origin’s backup and restore work in Blanc, so a backup file from another browser can be restored in its dashboard. Advanced settings that point to custom resource URLs stay blocked.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <aside class="truth-note" aria-labelledby="ubo-chrome-note-title"><p class="section-kicker">good to know</p><h2 id="ubo-chrome-note-title">Where it runs, and its limits.</h2><p>uBlock Origin is available for regular tabs on Apple Silicon and Intel Macs, Windows x64 and Linux x64. Private tabs always use Blanc Blocker, and so does the Intel build when it runs under Rosetta on an Apple Silicon Mac. Each profile keeps its own uBlock Origin settings, and they are not synced.</p><p>uBlock Origin is the one extension Blanc includes; Blanc does not install other browser extensions. Blanc can offer it only while its Electron runtime can load Manifest V2 extensions. If a later build cannot, Blanc switches to Blanc Blocker with a notice and keeps your uBlock Origin settings.</p><p>uBlock Origin is an independent open-source project under the GPLv3 license. Blanc ships it with its source, license notices and Blanc’s adaptation patches, and is not affiliated with the uBlock Origin project.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/gorhill/uBlock">uBlock Origin on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></aside>

  <section class="feature-close" aria-labelledby="ubo-chrome-close-title"><p class="section-kicker">keep the blocker you trust</p><h2 id="ubo-chrome-close-title">Full uBlock Origin, in a calmer browser.</h2><a class="cta" href="/download" data-track="feature_cta_click" data-feature="ublock-origin-after-chrome" data-cta-position="feature-close">download blanc</a></section>
</main>
